From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:58:01 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] PM: EM: retry the capacity update only for CPUs with a perf
 domain

em_check_capacity_update() walks every possible CPU and reschedules
itself a second later while any of them has no cpufreq policy. A CPU
that is never brought online never gets a policy, so the work runs once
a second forever. On an MT6797 board running only its two Cortex-A53
clusters, the two Cortex-A72 CPUs stay offline and a 120 s trace of the
idle, blanked system showed em_update_workfn 117 times.

A CPU without a perf domain has nothing to update. Look up the perf
domain first and only wait for the policy of a CPU that has one. A
cluster whose perf domain is registered later runs the check again from
em_dev_register_perf_domain().
---
 kernel/power/energy_model.c | 15 ++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel/power/energy_model.c b/kernel/power/energy_model.c
index e610cf8e9..d4a6ad54e 100644
--- a/kernel/power/energy_model.c
+++ b/kernel/power/energy_model.c
@@ -867,6 +867,16 @@ static void em_check_capacity_update(void)
 		if (cpumask_test_cpu(cpu, cpu_done_mask))
 			continue;
 
+		/*
+		 * A CPU without a perf domain has nothing to update. Waiting
+		 * for its policy would retry every second forever when it
+		 * never gets one, such as a CPU that is never brought online.
+		 */
+		dev = get_cpu_device(cpu);
+		pd = em_pd_get(dev);
+		if (!pd || em_is_artificial(pd))
+			continue;
+
 		policy = cpufreq_cpu_get(cpu);
 		if (!policy) {
 			failed_cpus++;
@@ -874,11 +884,6 @@ static void em_check_capacity_update(void)
 		}
 		cpufreq_cpu_put(policy);
 
-		dev = get_cpu_device(cpu);
-		pd = em_pd_get(dev);
-		if (!pd || em_is_artificial(pd))
-			continue;
-
 		cpumask_or(cpu_done_mask, cpu_done_mask,
 			   em_span_cpus(pd));
 
